00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.220 align:start position:0%
this morning the airforce will launch  the first of a powerful new generation  of GPS satellites the satellite is  nicknamed Vespucci after America's  namesake Explorer Amerigo Vespucci it  will blast off from Cape Canaveral  Florida aboard a SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket  now this is the first national security  launch for SpaceX mark Strassmann shows  us how the military mission benefits  billions of people on earth everyone  from pilots to first responders to  everyday drivers in the road an  estimated 4 billion people worldwide  rely on GPS now the US Air Force's  system of GPS satellites is about to get  a long-overdue makeover beginning with a  launch of this 577 million dollar  satellite GPS is really a military  system but it has provided incredible  capability for the everyday user the  satellite built by Lockheed Martin is  the first of 32 planned GPS 3 satellites  that will replace older ones in orbit  among its upgrades a stronger military  signal that's harder to jam and location  information that's three times more  accurate new satellites also have  civilian channels that will improve  everything from your ability to drive  your car around town to search and  rescue operations and the list goes on  and on still the launch comes four years  behind schedule and many of its key  features won't be fully up and running  for at least a few more years the  overarching reason they're running  behind schedule is the command and  control segment building the software  and the infrastructure on the ground  that can they can talk to these  satellites and do it all at a level of  encryption it's simply unprecedented  Lockheed Martin says today's liftoff  marks the first of what it hopes is a  steady flow of satellite launches with a  public feeling the impact of the new and  improved system by the end of 2020 for  CBS this morning  I'm mark Strassmann  look I'm all for that improvement  certainly using our ways and other  abilities GPS it helps me I use it every  day change our lives by 2020 we will  know where we're going down we have to  wait that long  enjoy the journey teehee
 

